What was adapted, and how it was changed:

  packages/pagedate/src/extract/patterns.ts
      NOT_A_DATE is adapted from htmldate's DISCARD_PATTERNS — the set of
      digit shapes that look like dates but are not (currency, phone numbers,
      IBANs, version strings). Reimplemented in TypeScript as a single
      alternation rather than a list of compiled patterns, and the version-
      number rule was narrowed to require a `v` prefix or a fourth component,
      because the original form also matched `16.12.2012`, the most common
      European date format.

  packages/pagedate/src/extract/context.ts
      The vocabulary of class and id tokens that mark article furniture was
      informed by htmldate's equivalent, though the scoring around it — the
      proximity rule, the marker tiers, the page-region distinction — is not
      derived from it.

